        "# Multimodal Fusion for Humanitarian Needs Classification\n",
        "\n",
        "**ST311 Deep Learning Project 2026 Group 8**\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook implements a multimodal deep learning framework combining xBD satellite imagery with CrisisMMD crisis tweets to classify humanitarian needs across four categories: infrastructure, medical, rescue, and other.\n",
        "\n",
        "We evaluate five model configurations: CNN baseline (image only), DistilBERT baseline (text only), late fusion, early fusion, and attention-based fusion across Hurricane Harvey and the 2017 Mexico Earthquake.\n",
        "\n",
        "**Data:** The xBD and CrisisMMD datasets are stored in our shared Google Drive folder (`ST311 Group Project/0. Dataset/`). The notebook expects this folder structure to be present. The datasets can be downloaded from [xBD](https://xview2.org/) and [CrisisMMD](https://crisisnlp.qcri.org/crisismmd).\n",
